open-source-core builds on WordCraft by the ArtCraft team and on craft-libs,
used as dependencies at pinned versions through the J. C. J. Foundation's forks
(docs/UPSTREAM.md). WordCraft and craft-libs are copyright (c) 2026 ArtCraft
Team and their contributors, MIT OR Apache-2.0. The fork carries changes of
ours, each recorded in docs/UPSTREAM.md.

The ArtCraft and WordCraft names, wordmarks and logos are not licensed to this
project and are not used by it. The plain-text credit above is the only
reference to them. Apps built on this core keep the credit "based on WordCraft
by the ArtCraft team" in their About page and README.

Portions of open-source-core were first written for Wordsmith Script
(github.com/jamescjfoundation/wordsmith-script, MIT OR Apache-2.0) and moved
here; see docs/review/script-29ed4bf.md.

Some Rust dependencies are under the Zlib, Unicode-3.0, IJG, BSL-1.0 and
CDLA-Permissive-2.0 licenses, as well as MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD and ISC. Each
crate's license is in its own package; docs/decisions/0001 lists which ones
and why. `cargo xtask third-party-licenses` writes every shipped dependency's
license text.
